        "notes": "Approximate present surviving Chihaya Castle earthwork ensemble: four principal enclosure grounds, southeastern enclosure, southwestern terrace, two current Chaya-no-dan outwork steps and narrow main-bailey northwest/west/south banks. Original current terrain shape and slope breaks retained. All nine bounded ground perimeters except the native lower-context ring are explicit authoring estimates; no archaeological survey, exact medieval edge/date or original grade is asserted. This is current ground form, not a restored medieval castle. Modern shrine/office/pavilion/Zondokan buildings, steles/signs/trees and undetectable lost ditch reconstructions are separate context; the whole natural hill is review terrain, not a castle solid."
